Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Description: Touch-friendly GNOME Files (Nautilus) for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 A patched build of GNOME Files (Nautilus) with touchscreen features:
  * long-press on the empty view background opens the context menu (the
    touch equivalent of a right click);
  * a "Show Select Boxes" preference (Files > Preferences > General) that
    shows a selection checkbox to the left of every file/folder, so several
    items can be selected on a touchscreen -- tap a box to toggle one item,
    or swipe a finger across the boxes to select/deselect several at once;
  * FILE DRAGS ARE ONE-FINGER ONLY: with a second or third finger on the
    glass (e.g. the 3-finger workspace swipe starting over an icon) the primary
    finger used to start a drag and MOVE THE FILES.  The view counts the live
    touch points (a GtkEventControllerLegacy in the capture phase) and
    on_item_drag_prepare() returns NULL -- cancelling the drag before GTK's
    gdk_drag_begin() -- while more than one finger is down.  Mouse and trackpad
    drags are unaffected.
 .
 Nautilus is C/GTK4, so this is a source patch, not an extension.  The
 package installs the patched /usr/bin/nautilus and its gschema by diverting
 Ubuntu's files (kept as *.erhai-orig); removing the package restores them.
 The build matches Ubuntu's debian/rules meson options (including
 -Dxdg-terminal-exec=true, so "Open in Terminal" is present).
 Package README: /usr/share/oneplus-erhai-nautilus/README.md

